      "latency_ms": 6313.4,
      "prompt_tokens": 25,
      "completion_tokens": 936,
      "output": "\n\nWater is a chemical substance composed of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom, forming the molecule **H₂O**. It is a fundamental component of life and exists in three primary states: **liquid** (as in rivers, lakes, and oceans), **solid** (as ice, when frozen), and **gas** (as water vapor, when heated). \n\n### Key Characteristics:\n1. **Chemical Structure**: Water molecules are **polar**, with a bent shape due to the uneven distribution of electrons. This polarity allows water to act as a **universal solvent**, dissolving many substances and facilitating chemical reactions in living organisms.\n\n2. **Physical Properties**:\n   - **High specific heat**: It absorbs and releases heat slowly, helping regulate temperature in organisms and environments.\n   - **Cohesion and adhesion**: Molecules stick to each other (cohesion) and to other surfaces (adhesion), enabling processes like capillary action in plants.\n   - **High surface tension**: Allows small organisms to walk on water and contributes to the formation of droplets.\n\n3. **Biological Role**: \n   - Essential for **cell function**, nutrient transport, and metabolic reactions.\n   - Makes up **60–70% of the human body** and is critical for hydration, digestion, and temperature regulation.\n\n4. **Environmental Significance**:\n   - Drives the **hydrological cycle** (evaporation, condensation, precipitation), shaping Earth's climate and ecosystems.\n   - Shapes landscapes through erosion and sediment transport.\n\n5. **Unique Properties**:\n   - Expands when frozen (ice is less dense than liquid water), allowing aquatic life to survive in cold climates.\n   - Colorless, odorless, and tasteless in its pure form, though impurities can alter these traits.\n\nWater’s versatility and essential role in sustaining life make it one of the most vital substances on Earth."
